  "title": "Collapse Order Status Periods into Ranges",
  "prompt": "An e-commerce platform tracks orders in two states: `processing_orders` holds rows for each day an order was in processing status, and `shipped_orders` holds rows for each day the same order was in shipped status. Every day between 2024-01-01 and 2024-01-31 is covered\u2014each order appears in exactly one table per day (no missing days). Your task is to collapse consecutive days of the same status into ranges. Write a query that produces one row per consecutive status period, showing `order_id`, `status` (either 'processing' or 'shipped'), `start_date`, and `end_date`. Order the output by `start_date` ascending. You may assume an order cannot switch back to a previous status; once shipped, it stays shipped.",
